  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Issue/unit: #26 / <verbatim|YM-000026>

    <item>Status: draft source audit; no theorem added

    <item>Scope: compare the reviewed free collinear classifier and
    internal-map erasure with the actual finite-grade application in
    <verbatim|YM.RG17.Joint> and <verbatim|YM.Bid.station>.

    <item>Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
    (<verbatim|source/upstream.json>).

    <item>Owned output: this audit file only.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Finding><label|finding>

  I found no type, grade, or same-object mismatch in the public finite-grade
  binding. The public route supplies the data consumed by
  <verbatim|YM.Bid.station> from one selected <verbatim|Run>;
  <verbatim|station> binds A01--A08 to the same hierarchy, response, Maxwell
  reference, and interaction. At each grade it chooses one scaling sequence
  after taking a finite maximum of the requests. The scale sequence may
  depend on the grade and finite test family. The resulting proportionality
  constant does not: <verbatim|YM.Climb.extends_form> compares the gradewise
  constants by injective grade inclusion, first above and then below its
  reference grade. The later stress normalization is a separate, explicit
  identification of the spin response with the same positional scalar and of
  the reference stress with the canonical free stress. It is not a
  consequence of the free classifier alone.

  The finite-test construction does not assert one uniform cutoff over all
  grades or all possible tests. At each fixed grade, the tests are finite;
  the source first takes the maximum of their finitely many scale thresholds.
  Grade uniformity needed for the scalar identity comes from the structural
  <verbatim|extends_form> argument, not from a diagonal choice of one scale
  working for all grades. The global configuration statement is then obtained
  at each fixed finite word/configuration by the analytic propagation
  theorem.

  <section|Exact source chain><label|exact-source-chain>

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG17/Joint.lean> starts from the purchased
    <verbatim|Run R>, calls <verbatim|R.bought>, and constructs the single
    table <verbatim|S>, final field package, and scaling supplier
    <verbatim|X>. The local response data are packaged as one
    <verbatim|Pert.Supplier> <verbatim|p> with fields <verbatim|I.p>,
    <verbatim|I.Y>, and the same selected <verbatim|M>. This is the actual
    public caller, rather than a separately selected <verbatim|Bourse> or
    comparison family.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Bid.station> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Town.lean>
    receives that same <verbatim|M,E,I,H> and <verbatim|p.uv>. Its
    <verbatim|witnessing> step combines A01, A02, A03, and
    <verbatim|YM.Outer.miles>; the resulting <verbatim|Shapes>,
    <verbatim|ShellCom>, <verbatim|Hyper>, and transverse conditions refer to
    <verbatim|I.p> and <verbatim|I.Y> on the selected table.

    <item>In <verbatim|YM.Bid.pressured>, each grade <verbatim|d> uses the
    selector <verbatim|W.lit.cuts> for <verbatim|M.T.W> and its reference
    spin structure. For that grade, A04, A05, and A06 provide
    <verbatim|Watches>. <verbatim|buysBoth> takes the maximum of the finite
    request bounds in these three records, and <verbatim|selects> uses
    <verbatim|ActLaw.connects> to choose one scaling object <verbatim|X>
    satisfying their conjunction. It is the same <verbatim|X> for the fitted
    derivative row, both A05 observer limits, and all rows in this grade's
    A06 selector.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Work.A06.test_aisle> gives the exact identity
    <verbatim|X.test k s (X.aisle k d q) = X.r k ^ s.m * scaledScene.lens q>;
    <verbatim|moves_limit> obtains convergence of the finite row map on fixed
    free vectors. <verbatim|transverse_zero> says the moved rows annihilate
    the actual derivative and <verbatim|I.p> exactly at every index. This is
    a common-kernel transfer, not an injectivity claim for the free scene
    family.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Climb.extends_form> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Climb/Peaks.lean> combines each gradewise
    <verbatim|concentrated> statement with nonvanishing of the derivative and
    response. <verbatim|fixed_kernel> gives a scalar at that grade. For any
    two grades above the reference threshold, <verbatim|over_peak> compares
    their scalars after raising the lower grade; injectivity of the inclusion
    and nonvanishing force equality. A grade below the threshold is compared
    by raising it to the fixed reference grade. Thus one nonzero real
    <verbatim|c> satisfies <verbatim|leaves I.p d = c \<bullet\> leaves
    V.deriv d> for every grade. The scale witnesses themselves need not be
    common across grades.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Bid.formed> turns that identity into
    <verbatim|Crystal>: it normalizes the same <verbatim|I.Y> by
    <verbatim|c^{-1}> and obtains the commutation and collinearity
    hypotheses. <verbatim|YM.Climb.descends> calls <verbatim|YM.Ward.global>
    on precisely this normalized spin row. Its hypotheses are
    <verbatim|DiffPlan.Derivatives>, <verbatim|Crystal.ready.1>
    (commutation), and <verbatim|Crystal.ready.2> (collinearity); the
    conclusion is <verbatim|Still> at every finite arity and every separated
    configuration.

    <item>A07 is applied to this same <verbatim|(V,M.T,J,H.spin,M.hT.spin)>.
    Its free input is the sibling Maxwell-data field <verbatim|M.frames :
    erases M.hT.spin M.T.W>, supplied by the free internal-map theorem. Its
    separate transfer input is the actual <verbatim|ActLaw> <verbatim|H.weak>
    (in the public caller, <verbatim|p.uv.weak>), aligned to this same
    <verbatim|M.T> and actual table. <verbatim|YM.Work.A07.transfer> works at
    each fixed grade on the finite dimensional real subspace
    <verbatim|Winds>, selects finitely many separating rows, and uses
    fixed-vector row convergence to get eventual injectivity. The threshold
    may depend on the grade. A08 only needs such a threshold:
    <verbatim|YM.Work.A08.answer> kills the Lie defect above it and uses
    injective grade inclusion to descend the bracket to every grade.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Bid.station> then packages the bracket result into
    <verbatim|Commission>; <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>
    obtains the station result and passes it into
    <verbatim|YM.Pert.withFinal>. Its private <verbatim|attached> proof
    identifies the <em|same> reference stress: from <verbatim|hM>,
    <verbatim|hK>, and <verbatim|hJ> it proves <verbatim|(M.T.\<kappa\>)^{-1}
    \<bullet\> M.T.J = freeStress>. The final <verbatim|YM.RG17.supplies>
    application therefore retains the one selected run and the same table for
    both the finite-grade station and the perturbative extension.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Interfaces checked against the prose
  units><label|interfaces-checked-against-the-prose-units>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  statement / canonical label>>|<cell|<strong|Exact source
  interface>>|<cell|<strong|Binding result>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|thm:free-collinear-scenes>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.scanner>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/MAXWELL/Scenes.lean>; it returns a finite
  <verbatim|Select> and <verbatim|Ens> for each grade <verbatim|d \<geq\>
  max(N,4)>>|<cell|Matches <verbatim|Lighthouse.Goes.cuts : \<exists\> n,
  \<forall\> d \<geq\> n, \<exists\> e, Ens e ...>; selectors and row counts
  may vary with <verbatim|d>.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|thm:free-quiet-classification>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.charges_quiet>,
  reached via <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.exposed> and
  <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.scanner>>|<cell|Its filtration is the full
  condition <verbatim|A_a(\<cal-P\>_k) \<subseteq\> \<cal-P\>_{k+1}> for
  every <verbatim|k \<leq\> d>, with signed/reality/vector conditions and
  unit annihilation. It concludes one scalar for all axes at each
  sufficiently large tested grade. The source quiet notion is all separated
  words of external-label capacity <verbatim|d>.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Climb.extends_form>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Climb/Peaks.lean>>|<cell|Converts
  gradewise finite comparisons to a grade-independent scalar using inclusion
  and nonzero derivative at a reference grade; no common scale witness is
  assumed.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|thm:free-internal-erasure> /
  <verbatim|sec:free-internal-ward-erasure>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.erasing>
  (<verbatim|Next/MAXWELL/AwayTeam.lean>), supplied to
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A07.answer>>|<cell|The stated alternating two-generator
  internal-map class matches <verbatim|Winds>; all rising/inclusion
  conditions are checked through the cutoff. A07 transports this class
  through the aligned grade isomorphism.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|thm:ward-global-propagation>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Ward.global>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Axis.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Still> holds for all
  finite word lengths, but only at separated configurations, which is exactly
  A08's domain.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|lem:ward-brackets>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A08.answer>>|<cell|Produces
  the bracket for every grade; high-grade erasure plus inclusion-injectivity
  handles lower grades.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|eq:angular-scalar-ratio> and
  <verbatim|sec:actual-stress-normalization>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Bid.pressured>,
  <verbatim|YM.Bid.services>, <verbatim|YM.Bid.formed>;
  <verbatim|YM.Climb.Lighthouse.Goes>>|<cell|The actual scalar <verbatim|c>
  is the response/derivative ratio; <verbatim|\<kappa\>> is the reference
  stress coefficient. A05's limits give <verbatim|c / X.xi \<rightarrow\>
  \<kappa\>> on the selected finite requests. They are not silently
  identified as equal constants. The same <verbatim|M.T.J> is later
  normalized against the canonical free stress in
  <verbatim|Joint.attached>.>>>>>

  The station's actual argument list contains A01--A11 and A13--A17; A12 is
  not passed to <verbatim|YM.Bid.station>. Nothing in this audit treats A12
  as a hidden premise. A14/A15/A17 and the later Lorentz/rotation
  construction are downstream of the finite-grade Ward binding and do not
  supply the free classifier.

  <section|Remaining qualification / risk><label|remaining-qualification--risk>

  This audit validates the object and quantifier joins, not the entirety of
  the large theorem. Its conclusion is conditional on the selected
  <verbatim|Run> and <verbatim|MaxwellData> producer hypotheses already
  discharged in their own units, including the Maxwell-data field
  <verbatim|M.frames>, finite-window jets, the A04--A06 observer receipts,
  the free classifier and free erasure. The prose must preserve their finite
  request quantifiers: for any fixed finite list of grades, arities, rows,
  and windows, take the maximum requested scale threshold before selecting
  the scale. It must not claim a threshold uniform over all grades or all
  configurations. The scalar's grade-uniformity is instead the exact
  <verbatim|extends_form> consequence described above.

  No mismatch was found between <verbatim|A01--A08>,
  <verbatim|YM.Bid.station>, and the <verbatim|Run.extractible17> caller. The
  remaining proof status is whatever the independent review records for those
  supplier units and the public <verbatim|Run> construction; this audit does
  not upgrade their status or assert that the full Yang--Mills proof has been
  independently accepted.

  <section|Evidence and checks><label|evidence-and-checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Inspected only the immediate selected route and interfaces:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG17/Joint.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/{Angular,Town}.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A01.lean>--<verbatim|A08.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Climb/{Beams,Peaks,Tests}.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/{Axis,Sum,Walk}.lean>, and
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/MAXWELL/Scenes.lean> plus the declarations named
    in the canonical free-classifier and internal-erasure evidence records.

    <item>Inspected the corresponding prose in
    <verbatim|physical-ward-propagation.tex> and
    <verbatim|physical-ward-free-classification.tex>; parent-owned
    angular-action and stress-normalization labels are treated only at their
    stated interface.

    <item>No Lean or LaTeX build was run. The only edit is this blueprint
    audit.

    <item><verbatim|git diff --no-index --check /dev/null
    \<less\>this-file\<gtr\>> emitted no whitespace diagnostics and returned
    status 1 because the file is new and untracked.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run; it stopped
    because the shared <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is
    absent in this draft clone.

    <item>No Lean or LaTeX build was run.
  </itemize-minus>

